  "solution": {
    "text": "Silicones with medium length chains behave as viscous oils, jellies and greases. They are chemically inert, i.e., resistant to oxidation. Since silicones are surrounded by non-polar alkyl groups, hence, are hydrophobic in nature. Being biocompatible, they are used in surgical and cosmetic implants. Hence, all options are correct."
